8.24.080
Discontinuance of use of flammable and combustible liquid tank(s).

A.  EVERY OWNER, OPERATOR, OR USER OF ANY TANK WHICH HAS BEEN
USED FOR THE STORAGE OF FLAMMABLE OR COMBUSTIBLE LIQUIDS, Any
person holding a business license shall, upon temporary or permanent discontinuance of the use
of a storage ANY SUCH tank or tanks, immediately notify the fire department, fire prevention
bureau, FIRE PREVENTION BUREAU OF THE FIRE DEPARTMENT in writing. and
dispose of storage tanks as directed by the city engineer and fire department, fire prevention
bureau,  EVERY REMOVAL AND EVERY DISPOSAL OF ANY SUCH TANK OR
TANKS WILL BE WITNESSED BY AN OFFICER FROM THE FIRE PREVENTION
BUREAU OF THE FIRE DEPARTMENT.  ANY SUCH REMOVAL OR DISPOSAL
which shall be in accordance with the provisions set forth in the standards of the National Fire
Protection Association for the storage, handling and use of flammable and combustible liquids,
"FLAMMABLE AND COMBUSTIBLE LIQUIDS CODE, Pamphlet No. 30”, Article 15 of
the Uniform Fire Code, Uniform Building Code, and Uniform Building Code Standard. AND
THE INTERNATIONAL FIRE CODE.  The word "temporary" does not mean the
discontinuance of the use of a tank(s) due to being out of a product for a short period or a closed
service station, if a diligent effort is made to secure a dealer or employee to re-open the facility.
After discontinuance for six months of the use of a tank(s), representatives of the city shall be
allowed to remove the tank(s) and charge the property owner for expenses involved.

B.   When old REMOVAL OR DISPOSAL OF ANY TANK USED FOR THE
STORAGE OF flammable and OR combustible liquids tank or tanks are to be removed as IS
required in BY the Uniform INTERNATIONAL Fire Code, THE REMOVAL AND
DISPOSAL MUST BE PERFORMED BY a licensed flammable and combustible liquids
contractor.  must be in charge of such removal.  However, EXCEPT THAT a qualified
contractor, when supervised by a licensed flammable and combustible liquids contractor, may
perform the removal of ANY such tank.(s).  When any old TANK USED FOR THE
STORAGE OF flammable and OR combustible liquids tank(s) are IS removed, all possible
liquids that remain in the tank(s) are to  SHALL be removed prior to any excavation.

8.24.100
Storage tank installation – Permits and inspection.

A.  Any person, persons, firm, association, partnership, or corporation desiring to install
ANY TANK OR RELATED EQUIPMENT FOR THE STORAGE OF ANY flammable and
OR combustible liquid, equipment AS designated in this chapter either above or below ground,
must obtain a permit from the city engineer CHIEF BUILDING OFFICIAL and pay the
applicable fee as established by the table of building permit fees in the latest edition of the
Uniform Building Code adopted by the city. CITY CODE SECTION 15.08.030.  The fee
assessed will be for each storage tank.  Application for storage tank permits must be
accompanied by accurate plats or drawings showing the lot or tract of land, with the location,
size and description of each tank, the layout of fill and vent pipes, the location and size of pump
and specifications for the construction of each tank, its connections, fittings, openings, and safety
appliances.
