C.  No tank or piping shall be buried or otherwise covered up until the tank has been air
tested under the provisions in National Fire Protection Association Pamphlet No. 30 and the tank
or AND any RELATED piping AND EQUIPMENT HAVE has been inspected and approved
by the city engineer CHIEF BUILDING OFFICIAL and the fire department, fire prevention
bureau. FIRE PREVENTION BUREAU OF THE FIRE DEPARTMENT.

D.  The city engineer CHIEF BUILDING OFFICIAL or fire department, fire prevention
bureau  THE FIRE PREVENTION BUREAU OF THE FIRE DEPARTMENT, will require
any flammable and combustible liquid equipment be uncovered, at the owner's expense, if
repairs or replacement are necessary or if they have been covered unlawfully.

8.24.110
Violations – Penalty.

A.   Any person violating any of the provisions of this chapter pertaining to flammable and
OR combustible liquids, or who has not received a proper license or permit shall be issued a stop
work order and assessed a maximum penalty of two hundred dollars ($200.00) or ninety (90)
days in jail.  AS DIRECTED BY THE CHIEF BUILDING OFFICIAL PURSUANT TO
THE MOST RECENTLY ADOPTED VERSION OF THE INTERNATIONAL
BUILDING CODE.

B.   ANY PERSON VIOLATING THE PROVISIONS OF THIS CHAPTER, OR
CAUSING THE PROVISIONS OF THIS CHAPTER TO BE VIOLATED, WILL BE
GUILTY OF A MISDEMEANOR PUNISHABLE PURSUANT TO THE GENERAL
PENALTY PROVISION PROVIDED FOR IN SECTION 1.24.010 OF CITY CODE.

Section 4.  That Chapter 8.28, Portable Fire Extinguishers and Hose Station Equipment, is
amended as follows:

8.28.020
Business license required.

Every person who services and tests portable fire extinguishers and hose station equipment
for compensation is required to obtain a business license.  The license must state specifically
whether it is issued for portable fire extinguishers or hose station equipment, or both.
Applications, with nonrefundable annual licensing fee of ninety dollars ($90.00), must be
submitted to the office of city clerk.  Upon approval by the FIRE CHIEF OF THE FIRE
DEPARTMENT AND mayor or city council, the city clerk will issue a license which will be
effective for one year from date of issuance.  General licensing provisions set forth in CITY
CODE Chapter 5.04 apply to this type of license.

8.28.030
Servicing and testing.

All persons licensed must service and test all portable fire extinguishers and hose station
equipment in accordance with the Uniform INTERNATIONAL Fire Code Standards, as
adopted and referenced in Chapter 8.12.
```

### Page 5 of 5

```text
8.28.050
Examination.

A.  Applicants for a portable fire extinguisher and hose station equipment license are
required to pass a written examination administered by the fire department OR SUBMIT
PROOF OF RECOGNIZED CERTIFICATION TO BE APPROVED BY THE FIRE
PREVENTION BUREAU OF THE FIRE DEPARTMENT.  The examination may be
supplemented by practical tests or demonstrations deemed necessary to determine the applicant's
knowledge and ability to service portable fire extinguishers and hose station equipment.  The
results of the examination shall be forwarded to the office of city clerk to accompany the license
application.

8.28.060
Insurance.

All persons licensed are required to maintain current public GENERAL liability insurance
equal to the minimum amount required of all other contractors pursuant to the provisions of
CITY CODE Chapter 5.44, Contractors.

Section 5.  That Chapter 8.32, Gasoline and Oil Dispensing Equipment, is amended as
follows:

8.32.020
Protection of equipment.

All pumps or other mechanical measuring devices used for retailing or dispensing gasoline
must be securely locked so that no fluid can be withdrawn, except when the operation of pumps
or other devices is under the supervision and in charge of an attendant.

Section 6.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon approval and publication
but not sooner than November 1, 2013.

